# The IAM module (services/iam/, .kiro/specs/iam-compatible-auth/).
# Sourced from the top-level Kconfig's "Service Modules" menu.

config IAM
	bool "IAM-compatible authentication and authorization service"
	default n
	depends on OPENSSL
	help
	  Builds the services/iam/ module: an AWS IAM-compatible service
	  (users, groups, roles, managed and inline policies, access keys,
	  STS) hosted by its own Raft group, and the policy evaluator that
	  front ends such as the Redis gateway embed to authorize requests
	  locally. So far the module holds the policy parser and matchers
	  (task 10) and their tests; the state machine, evaluator, daemon and
	  Query API follow. OpenSSL is needed for the access-key sealing and
	  SigV4 the later tasks add. Off by default like every new module
	  (services/README.md). See .kiro/specs/iam-compatible-auth/.
